==Spanish==
{{wikipedia|lang=es}}

===Etymology===
{{unk|es}}. One theory is that it was coined by Spanish colonists based upon the name of the local chief at that time, {{cog|nci|Nicarao||[[w:Nicarao|Nicarao]]}} + {{m|es|agua||water}}. Another is that it may have meant ‘surrounded by water’ in an indigenous language. (This could either be a reference to its two large freshwater lakes, Lake Nicaragua and Lake Managua, or to the fact that it bounded on the east and the west by oceans.)

===Pronunciation===
